### Recorder database

The chart can run the recorder database next to Home Assistant on the official
`mariadb` or `postgres` image (enable one of them). It creates a StatefulSet,
a Service and a Secret, and sets `RECORDER_DB_URL` on the Home Assistant
container. Point the recorder at it in `configuration.yaml`:

```yaml
recorder:
  db_url: !env_var RECORDER_DB_URL
```

```yaml
mariadb:
  enabled: true
  auth:
    existingSecret: home-assistant-db   # keys: password, root-password
```

Pinned versions follow what Home Assistant supports: MariaDB on an LTS series
(10.11, 11.4, 11.8 or 12.3) and PostgreSQL 15 or newer. Renovate keeps the
images within MariaDB 12.3 and PostgreSQL 18; moving to a new PostgreSQL major
needs a dump and restore. The password is embedded in `RECORDER_DB_URL`, so it
must be URL-safe.

**Upgrading from 2.x:** the Bitnami `mariadb` and `postgresql` subcharts were
removed (Bitnami's free images are only published as `latest`). Their values
and data layout are not compatible; dump the database before upgrading and
restore it into the new StatefulSet.
{{- end -}}